  "notes": "Claimed here on `west-coast-club`'s explicit hand-off. The tempo spine is the largest in the batch and the entry lists it title by title; the trap-facing bulk is the 101–137 read band folding to 51–69 felt, so that band is `session.bpm` and `halfTime` is true. The named keys are authored exactly — F minor, D♭, B♭ minor and F♯ — and `scales` carries `major` because the entry names D♭ major and F♯ major alongside the minors. Harmony is the entry's two-sided claim: \"two-chord minor loops for the trap material against genuine 4-chord 90s-R&B cycles with cadences for the retro material\", so both shapes are families rather than one. The kit is the first of her three, with the finger-snap and live-percussion overlay the entry says \"run through all three\". The melody carries the sentence that actually distinguishes her: \"mid-alto with a rap-adjacent rhythmic delivery in the verses and full singing on the hooks\" — a moderate density with a wide phrase range rather than a fixed one. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the swing amount, every drum probability and density, the 808 slide numbers, and the melody density band; the entry marks drum detail as lane inference. ⚠ `confidence` is medium — the research rates it high-medium, which this dataset maps to medium. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state.",
